WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:08.170
This was named after Glen T. Seaborg, who
was an American chemist, who was the pioneer

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:16.350
of the chemistry of plutonium and all the
radioactive elements. He worked in Berkley,

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:25.300
California, and died quite recently in the
late 1990s, and there is a memorial lecture

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:33.670
that was set up in his honour and I was fortunate
in 2004 to be the Seaborg Memorial Lecturer

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:39.190
and I went and I saw the building where he
had worked and gave lectures though not about

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:42.070
his element because that is not really my
area of chemistry.

